dem-huge.gls -- dem-huge.txt (made by: sh dem-make.sh huge)

The file: 18,000,000 lines "huge NNNNNNNN: ção € 😀 a line of a file of
more than a gigabyte" (1.28 GB): above the 1 GB at which C-x C-f opens a
file in shards of 16 MB by itself.

Open:   chezweb, then C-x C-f dem-huge.txt RET
1. Expect: "Shard 1/77", within some seconds (the index is built in
   one pass); the mode line shows [1/77].
2. C-c C-v n  C-c C-v p  Expect: the next shard and back, within 1 s each.
3. C-c C-v g 40 RET      Expect: shard 40.
4. M-g 17999999 RET    Expect: that line, in the last shard.
5. Searching across shards.  C-s searches only the shard on screen;
   when it fails there, C-s once more searches the shards AFTER it,
   never the ones before (it does not wrap around to shard 1).
   a. C-c C-v g 40 RET, then C-s huge 17999990 (do not press RET)
      Expect: "Failing Search forward: huge 17999990" (it is in the last shard).
      Press C-s again.
      Expect: "Searching shard 41/77...", up to 77/77, then the cursor
      just after "huge 17999990", in the last shard.  RET ends the search.
   b. From there, C-s huge 00000001, then C-s again
      Expect: still failing, at once: that line is in shard 1, before
      the last, and there are no shards after the last.  C-g returns
      the cursor to where the search started.
6. C-c C-v [  then  XYZ  then  C-x C-s
   Expect: the whole file written again with XYZ at its start, within a
   minute; then in a terminal:  head -c 20 dem-huge.txt
7. Make it again afterwards:  sh dem-make.sh huge
